--- !u!114 &1159643599
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1159643596}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3269ab77e5738674b9fefab358f453ff, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::UIAnimLab.Station
  Code: T16
  Title: 'Custom Property: numbers'
  Summary: Custom Property on a C# float and int (the gauge's Health and Coins),
    and on a text counted as a number or typed out.
  Watch: Gauge, Score, Typed
  WatchObjects:
  - {fileID: 232942574}
  - {fileID: 2117097034}
  - {fileID: 806594361}
  HowTo: Play <b>Heal</b>, <b>Count Up</b> and <b>Type</b>. Stop and Restore afterwards.
    Then open the <b>Property</b> dropdown on Heal's first step.
  Expect: Heal fills the bar from 10 to 100 HP while Coins counts in whole numbers
    to 250. Count Up counts from 120 to 15,000 with a thousands separator. Type writes
    the line letter by letter, and the bold tag inside it never shows half-typed.
    Stop and Restore puts back 75 HP, 12 coins, 120 and an empty line. The dropdown
    lists Health and Coins under TestGauge, but not HealthFraction (read-only), OldHealth
    ([Obsolete]) or IsAlive (a bool).
  Needs: 1
  Style: 0
  WikiPage: 
  Capture: 
  Width: 620
  StageHeight: 300
  Header: {fileID: 327826089}
  Stage: {fileID: 1890636373}
  Footer: {fileID: 1121821032}
  TitleText: {fileID: 1684844091}
  BadgeText: {fileID: 314113098}
  SummaryText: {fileID: 211503920}
  WatchText: {fileID: 446542215}
  HowToText: {fileID: 1454825921}
  ExpectText: {fileID: 290451418}
